<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">conviction</ansi>

Conviction is your force of will made fuel -- the third of your three
resource pools, alongside Health and Stamina. Where Stamina powers the
body, Conviction powers belief and presence: the will to bend a fight --
and, on Gaius, reality itself -- to your intent. Most games have two pools;
this is the one that is new, so it is worth understanding early.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What Conviction Powers ━━━</ansi>

  - <ansi fg="stat">Spellcasting</ansi> -- every spell you cast draws on your Conviction.
  - <ansi fg="stat">Rhetoric in combat</ansi> -- taunts, and the rally and warcry battle-shouts.
  - <ansi fg="stat">Conviction-channel attacks</ansi> -- strikes that lean on presence, not muscle.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Running Low ━━━</ansi>

As your Conviction drains, the things it powers weaken with it:
  - Your spells bite less deeply.
  - Your taunts land less often and hold less firmly.
  - Rally and warcry lose their force.

A caster or a taunt-focused fighter who lets Conviction bottom out is as
spent as a swordsman out of Stamina -- the tools still cost you, but they
no longer land like they should. When it runs dry, break off and recover.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Regeneration ━━━</ansi>

Conviction returns a little each round, and much faster while you are out
of combat and at rest -- the same rhythm as Health and Stamina. Rest, or
flee a fight you are losing, to bring it back before you commit again.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Raising It ━━━</ansi>

Your maximum Conviction deepens with the force-of-will stats behind it --
Willpower and Charisma -- which, like everything on Gaius, grow through
use. Cast, persuade, and command, and the pool that fuels them widens.

